This is not something to change in NetHack. The terminal only has a
very limited set colors and programs (such as NetHack) can tell it to
use one of them. In many Windows versions, it seems the default
setting for the terminal colour blue is a bit dark. You can change
that by clicking "properties" (or some such) in the console window
control box (left of the title bar) or by making a shorcut for NetHack
and editing it (again IIRC by clicking on properties from a pop-up
menu in explorer).

